    "body": "## Security/privacy impact\n\nAfter suspended accounts were hidden from public profile and public review reads, `PUT /user-blocks/{userId}` still resolved an arbitrary numeric target through global `UserRepository.findById(...)`. A caller could therefore distinguish a missing id from a suspended existing account and, on success or an existing block, receive that account's nickname through `UserBlockResponse`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- resolve block targets only through `findByIdAndStatus(userId, ACTIVE)`;\n- perform that ACTIVE-account lookup before consulting an existing block relation, so a repeated block request cannot reveal a target that was suspended after the relation was created;\n- return the existing neutral user-not-found response for both missing and suspended targets;\n- ensure unavailable targets fail before block-relation lookup or persistence;\n- preserve self-block rejection and idempotent behavior for ACTIVE targets;\n- leave the user's private existing block list and unblock flow unchanged, so established safety relationships remain manageable.\n\nNo authentication/session, job lifecycle, escrow, wallet, payout, schema, or moderation-state behavior is changed.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n- successful blocking proves the ACTIVE-scoped lookup is used and global `findById` is not;\n- idempotent blocking of an ACTIVE target keeps the same behavior while still enforcing the scoped lookup first;\n- self-blocking fails before target/relation lookup;\n- suspended or unknown targets fail before relation lookup/save and cannot fall back to global lookup;\n- both account-access and user-blocking documentation record the privacy boundary.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after every relevant workflow is green on the exact current PR head SHA. Immediately before merge, revalidate the head SHA, review threads and current `master`; if `master` moved, integrate it safely and rerun the exact-head gate. Merge with a merge commit only, then verify the merge parents and all post-merge workflows.",
